# All chats (desktop parity slice 4; Boss approved design/soma-all-chats-mockup.html, 2026-10-28): the strip's "all" opens
# every chat and thread, with a search; over the chat on the cover, beside it unfolded; Back closes it. The fictional chat
# fixture runs production OmaChatScreen. Prerequisite: -PartifactPreview :artifact-preview:assembleDebug installed.
fold folded
rotate portrait
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview
launch dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity
tap Show the tabs
expect all
tap All chats
expect Search chats
expect Fold
# Look: All chats over the whole cover: the search field, TODAY, the Fold row with its last words; nothing cut at the edges.
shot cover-all-chats
tap Search chats
type tests
expect running the tests
# Look: "tests" marked in the Fold row's words, and "1 of 1 chat match" under it.
shot cover-all-chats-search
key BACK
key BACK
absent Search chats
# Look: back to the chat; the list closed.
shot cover-all-chats-closed
fold open
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview
launch dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity
tap Show the tabs
tap All chats
expect Search chats
# Look: All chats beside the chat, the chat still in view on the left.
shot unfolded-all-chats
key BACK
[phone] On the Fold: "all" in the strip lists his chats and the Mac's threads, older ones too; a search finds one by a word in it; tapping it opens it, an archived one comes back
